    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1243">

                <pb facs="1217" n="1051" xml:id="pg1051"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/411</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Fletcher to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-17T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 17, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Your telegram March 15, 6 p.m. Minister of Fomento appreciates difficulties
                    American mine owners will have in complying with decree in the time allowed and
                    will take up the whole mining question very soon with the First Chief who is now
                    in the Capital. Indications are that an extension will be granted. Translation
                    of the decree referred to sent you in last Wednesday’s pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
